@startuml
!include theme.iuml
left to right direction
title Hosted business user goals and supporting services
actor "Visitor (signed out)" as Visitor
actor "Account owner (signed in)" as Owner
actor "Email service" as Mail
actor "Google identity service" as Google
actor "Gemini provider" as AI
rectangle "Mboa private language workspace" {
  usecase "Register and verify email" as Register
  usecase "Sign in with password" as Login
  usecase "Sign in / explicitly link Google" as OAuth
  usecase "Recover password" as Recover
  usecase "Manage private projects\nand terminology" as Terms
  usecase "Record / attach / play audio" as Audio
  usecase "Review terminology approval" as Review
  usecase "Preview documents or media" as Preview
  usecase "Consented cloud transcription" as Cloud
  usecase "Translate with source labels" as Translate
  usecase "Optional AI suggestion" as Suggest
  usecase "Search reference dictionary" as Dictionary
  usecase "Ask the business assistant" as Chat
  usecase "Save / reopen / export /\ndelete selected work" as History
  usecase "Restore a terminology revision" as Revision
  usecase "Create / schedule / download backup" as Backup
  usecase "Preview and confirm workspace restore" as Restore
  usecase "Validate archive integrity\nand record limits" as Validate
}
Visitor -- Register
Visitor -- Login
Visitor -- OAuth
Visitor -- Recover
Owner -- OAuth
Owner -- Terms
Owner -- Audio
Owner -- Review
Owner -- Preview
Owner -- Translate
Owner -- Dictionary
Owner -- Chat
Owner -- History
Owner -- Revision
Owner -- Backup
Owner -- Restore
Mail -- Register
Mail -- Recover
Google -- OAuth
AI -- Suggest
AI -- Cloud
AI -- Chat
Suggest ..> Translate : <<extend>>\n[no exact answer and AI enabled]
Cloud ..> Preview : <<extend>>\n[needed and explicitly consented]
Backup ..> Validate : <<include>>
Restore ..> Validate : <<include>>
note bottom of Owner
  These are session states, not team-access roles.
  Private goals require a verified account.
  Saved does not mean approved.
end note
legend bottom
  Include points to mandatory reused behavior; extend points to its base use case.
  Preview never automatically saves or approves terminology.
  Scheduling requires a running server; infrastructure operations are not an in-app admin role.
endlegend
@enduml
